    <briefdescription>
<para>This module provides an adapter for Lua/C API to generate box.info() and index:info() introspection trees. </para>    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>The primary purpose of this adapter is to eliminate Engine &lt;-&gt; Lua interdependency.</para><para>TREE STRUCTURE</para><para>{ <ndash/> info_begin section = { <ndash/> info_begin_table key1 = int; <ndash/> info_append_int key2 = double; <ndash/> info_append_double key3 = str; <ndash/> info_append_str }; <ndash/> info_end_table</para><para>section2 = { ... }; ... } <ndash/> info_end</para><para>IMPLEMENTATION DETAILS</para><para>Current implementation calls Lua/C API under the hood without any pcall() wrapping. As you may now, idiosyncratic Lua/C API unwinds C stacks on errors in a way you can&apos;t handle in C. Please ensure that all blocks of code which call info_append_XXX() functions are exception/longjmp safe. </para>    </detaileddescription>
